diff --git a/docs/bots.md b/docs/bots.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6709897
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/bots.md
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+## Chat Bots Architecture & Design Notes
+
+### Data Model
+
+Bots are modeled as `User` records (`role: :bot`, see `app/models/user/bot.rb` and `app/models/user/role.rb`):
+
+- **`users.role`**: `enum :role, %i[ member administrator bot ]` (`2` = `bot`).
+- **`users.bot_token`**: 24-character base58 random credential generated via `generate_unique_secure_token` on creation (`nil` for human users and cleared to `nil` when a bot is deactivated).
+- **`users.creator_id`**: nullable self-referential foreign key (`on_delete: :nullify`) tracking which chat member created the bot.
+- **`users.password_digest`**: nullable so bots cannot authenticate via password/session login.
+
+Modeling bots on `User` means bots reuse existing `Membership`, `Room`, `Message` (`creator_id` FK to `users`), `User::Avatar`, `Message::Broadcasts`, and `Room::MessagePusher` pipelines without polymorphism or schema duplication:
+
+- **Open rooms**: `User#grant_membership_to_open_rooms` (`after_create_commit`) and `Rooms::Open#grant_access_to_all_users` include active bots automatically.
+- **Closed & direct rooms**: `Rooms::ClosedsController`, `Rooms::DirectsController`, and `Autocompletable::UsersController` query `User.active`, allowing bots to be added to rooms the same way as people.
+- **Human-only surfaces**: `User.without_bots` excludes bots from the `/account/edit` member management list, session login/transfer, IP bans, and direct-message sidebar placeholders.
+- **Soft deletion**: Deleting a bot calls `User#deactivate`, setting `status: :deactivated`, clearing `bot_token: nil`, and removing non-direct room memberships while keeping historical messages authored by the bot intact.
+
+### Ownership & Authorization
+
+- Any signed-in member can access `/bots`, `/bots/new`, and `POST /bots`.
+- `/bots` (`BotsController#index`) lists `Current.user.bots.active` for regular members and `User.active_bots` for administrators on a single page without pagination, with `Cache-Control: no-store` and `turbo-cache-control: no-store`.
+- `User::Role#can_administer?(record)` returns `false` for bots themselves, `true` for administrators, and `true` when `self == record&.creator`, authorizing `edit`, `update`, and `destroy` on `BotsController`.
+
+### Bot Code & HTTP Messaging API
+
+- **Bot code format**: `"#{id}-#{bot_token}"` (`User#bot_key`). `User.authenticate_bot` verifies numeric `id`, active bot status, and compares the full `bot_key` via `ActiveSupport::SecurityUtils.secure_compare`.
+- **Log hygiene**: `:bot_code` (alongside `:token` and `:_key`) is filtered in `config/initializers/filter_parameter_logging.rb`.
+- **Endpoint**: `POST /rooms/:room_id/:bot_code/messages` (`Bots::MessagesController#create`).
+  - Inherits from `ActionController::Base` (including `ActiveStorage::SetCurrent`, `BlockBannedRequests`, `SetCurrentRequest`, `VersionHeaders`) so CLI User-Agents are never blocked by browser version gates.
+  - Overrides `self.dispatch` for non-multipart requests to set `action_dispatch.request.request_parameters = {}` so raw shell payloads sent via `curl -d "..."` (`application/x-www-form-urlencoded`) containing `%`, `&`, or arbitrary bytes never trigger `ActionController::BadRequest` before reaching the action, and raw message text is kept out of parameter logs.
+  - Reads `request.raw_post` as UTF-8, HTML-escapes text, converts newlines to `<br>`, and creates the message via `@room.messages.create_with_attachment!`.
+  - Responds `401 Unauthorized` (invalid/revoked bot code, checked before room lookup to avoid room ID enumeration), `404 Not Found` (unknown room or bot not a member of the room), `422 Unprocessable Content` (blank body and no attachment, enforced by `Message#ensure_has_content`), or `201 Created` with `Location: /messages/:message_id`.
+
+### Notes for Future Extensions
+
+- **`Location: /messages/:message_id`**: Returning `/messages/:message_id` provides a canonical message identifier that future bot endpoints (e.g., bot message updates, deletions, or file/attachment endpoints) can target while verifying `message.creator == authenticated_bot`.
+- **Attachments**: `Message#ensure_has_content` and `Bots::MessagesController#message_params` already coordinate with `Message::Attachment` (`create_with_attachment!`), making dedicated multipart or binary file-upload extensions straightforward.
diff --git a/test/controllers/bots/messages_controller_test.rb b/test/controllers/bots/messages_controller_test.rb
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..331dbac
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/controllers/bots/messages_controller_test.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,168 @@
+require "test_helper"
+
+class Bots::MessagesControllerTest < ActionDispatch::IntegrationTest
+  setup do
+    host! "chat.example.com"
+    @bot = User.bot.create!(name: "Deploy Bot", creator: users(:kevin))
+    @open_room = rooms(:hq)
+    @closed_room = rooms(:designers)
+  end
+
+  test "posting raw text creates a message authored by the bot and returns 201 with Location" do
+    assert_difference -> { @open_room.messages.count }, +1 do
+      post room_bot_messages_url(@open_room, @bot.bot_key),
+        params: +"Deploy of v1.2.3 finished ✅",
+        headers: { "Content-Type" => "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" }
+    end
+
+    message = Message.last
+    assert_response :created
+    assert_equal "/messages/#{message.id}", response.headers["Location"]
+    assert_equal @bot, message.creator
+    assert_equal "Deploy Bot", message.creator.name
+    assert_equal "Deploy of v1.2.3 finished ✅", message.plain_text_body
+  end
+
+  test "handles raw bodies with percent signs, ampersands, angle brackets, newlines, and invalid JSON" do
+    payload = +"Build #42: 98% pass & 2 < 3 in <main>\n{\"raw\": broken"
+
+    post room_bot_messages_url(@open_room, @bot.bot_key),
+      params: payload,
+      headers: { "Content-Type" => "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" }
+
+    assert_response :created
+    message = Message.last
+    assert_equal payload, message.plain_text_body
+
+    sign_in :david
+    get room_url(@open_room)
+    assert_response :ok
+    assert_select "##{dom_id(message)}" do
+      assert_select ".message__author strong", text: "Deploy Bot"
+      assert_select ".trix-content", text: /Build #42: 98% pass & 2 < 3 in <main>/
+    end
+  end
+
+  test "escapes script tags safely" do
+    post room_bot_messages_url(@open_room, @bot.bot_key),
+      params: +"<script>alert('xss')</script>",
+      headers: { "Content-Type" => "text/plain" }
+
+    assert_response :created
+    message = Message.last
+
+    sign_in :david
+    get room_url(@open_room)
+    assert_select "##{dom_id(message)} script", count: 0
+    assert_select "##{dom_id(message)} .trix-content", text: /<script>alert\('xss'\)<\/script>/
+  end
+
+  test "broadcasts message to connected clients and unread rooms channel" do
+    assert_broadcasts UnreadRoomsChannel.stream_name_for(users(:david).id), 1 do
+      post room_bot_messages_url(@open_room, @bot.bot_key),
+        params: +"Deploy of v1.2.3 finished ✅",
+        headers: { "Content-Type" => "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" }
+    end
+
+    assert_rendered_turbo_stream_broadcast @open_room, :messages, action: "append", target: [ @open_room, :messages ] do
+      assert_select ".message__author strong", text: "Deploy Bot"
+      assert_select ".message__body", text: /Deploy of v1.2.3 finished ✅/
+    end
+  end
+
+  test "triggers push notifications just like a human-authored message" do
+    expected_deliveries = Push::Subscription.joins(user: :memberships)
+      .merge(Membership.visible.disconnected.involved_in_everything.where(room: @open_room))
+      .count
+    assert expected_deliveries > 0
+
+    perform_enqueued_jobs only: Room::PushMessageJob do
+      WebPush.expects(:payload_send).with { |params|
+        payload = JSON.parse(params[:message])
+        payload["title"] == @open_room.name &&
+          payload.dig("options", "body") == "Deploy Bot: Deploy of v1.2.3 finished ✅"
+      }.times(expected_deliveries)
+
+      post room_bot_messages_url(@open_room, @bot.bot_key),
+        params: +"Deploy of v1.2.3 finished ✅",
+        headers: { "Content-Type" => "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" }
+    end
+
+    start = Time.now
+    pool = Rails.configuration.x.web_push_pool.delivery_pool
+    sleep 0.01 while pool.completed_task_count < expected_deliveries && Time.now - start < 0.5
+    assert_equal expected_deliveries, pool.completed_task_count
+  end
+
+  test "returns 422 Unprocessable Content for empty or whitespace-only body without attachment" do
+    assert_no_difference -> { Message.count } do
+      post room_bot_messages_url(@open_room, @bot.bot_key),
+        params: +"",
+        headers: { "Content-Type" => "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" }
+    end
+    assert_response :unprocessable_content
+
+    assert_no_difference -> { Message.count } do
+      post room_bot_messages_url(@open_room, @bot.bot_key),
+        params: +"   \n  ",
+        headers: { "Content-Type" => "text/plain" }
+    end
+    assert_response :unprocessable_content
+  end
+
+  test "returns 404 Not Found for bad room id or room the bot is not a member of" do
+    post room_bot_messages_url(999999, @bot.bot_key),
+      params: +"Hello",
+      headers: { "Content-Type" => "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" }
+    assert_response :not_found
+
+    post room_bot_messages_url("bad.room", @bot.bot_key),
+      params: +"Hello",
+      headers: { "Content-Type" => "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" }
+    assert_response :not_found
+
+    assert_not_includes @closed_room.users, @bot
+    post room_bot_messages_url(@closed_room, @bot.bot_key),
+      params: +"Hello",
+      headers: { "Content-Type" => "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" }
+    assert_response :not_found
+
+    @closed_room.memberships.grant_to(@bot)
+    post room_bot_messages_url(@closed_room, @bot.bot_key),
+      params: +"Hello closed room!",
+      headers: { "Content-Type" => "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" }
+    assert_response :created
+  end
+
+  test "returns 401 Unauthorized for invalid bot code or deleted bot" do
+    post room_bot_messages_url(@open_room, "invalid-bot-code"),
+      params: +"Hello",
+      headers: { "Content-Type" => "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" }
+    assert_response :unauthorized
+
+    post room_bot_messages_url(999999, "invalid.code"),
+      params: +"Hello",
+      headers: { "Content-Type" => "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" }
+    assert_response :unauthorized
+
+    old_key = @bot.bot_key
+    @bot.deactivate
+
+    post room_bot_messages_url(@open_room, old_key),
+      params: +"Hello after delete",
+      headers: { "Content-Type" => "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" }
+    assert_response :unauthorized
+  end
+
+  test "supports posting an attachment with empty body" do
+    assert_difference -> { @open_room.messages.count }, +1 do
+      post room_bot_messages_url(@open_room, @bot.bot_key),
+        params: { attachment: fixture_file_upload("moon.jpg", "image/jpeg") }
+    end
+
+    assert_response :created
+    message = Message.last
+    assert message.attachment?
+    assert_equal "/messages/#{message.id}", response.headers["Location"]
+  end
+end
